id: 4-2-airship
name: WORLD 4-2
world: 4
stage: 2
theme: airship-deck
music: airship
time: 300
start: 2,6
startMode: stand
;; SMB3 auto-scroll (world/camera.ts); the campaign boards up 4-2's anchor chain at column 2 onto
;; the bow platform (column 3, row 7: keep it solid with headroom above).
camera: auto
scroll: 0.375
parent: 4-2

;; Larry Koopa's airship, the deck (0.5.0), laid out after SMB3 World 1's airship (owner's
;; reference), all art and music original. The camera scrolls on its own (0.375 px/f: about
;; 58 s from the bow to the stern) and stops at the stern.
;; - BOW (0-32): a raised bow platform (row 7, the start) over the stair-stepped prow, the fore
;;   deck (row 9) with two cannons aimed up-left (14, 22), a Rocky Wrench manhole (18), a short
;;   post with a Bullet Bill blaster at its right end (28-30) right against the tall post (31-32,
;;   3 high; together a staircase with no pocket to be trapped in) where the deck steps down. A
;;   propeller turns under the prow's bottom hull (23).
;; - MIDDLE (33-70): the long low main deck (row 12) on two hull segments with a 2-wide gap
;;   (50-51), a propeller behind each (49, 65); a 3-tall blaster post (44, its Bullet Bills flying
;;   just over a standing hero's head), a plain post (59) and a ? block (55, row 7: 5 rows above
;;   the deck so a Bullet Bill can be jumped under it; mushroom, or fire flower when big). Above
;;   it the plank overhang (row 3, 40-60) with cannons hanging under it aimed down-left (43, 49)
;;   and a three-cannon turret (56-57: left, right and down-left, so nothing crosses fire over
;;   the gap), and at its right end the thick block (61-75, rows 3-5) over the metal gateway
;;   (61-68, not solid; iron struts `t` frame it).
;; - STERN (71-97): the lower deck (row 13) with a Rocky Wrench (77, well clear of where the hero
;;   drops in), then four 2-wide steps up (83-90) to the high stern deck (row 8, 91-97): a
;;   railing, portholes in the hull (`%`), a propeller under it, and THE PIPE (94) down into
;;   Larry's room (4-2-larry).
;; Cannon cells are solid (the cannon fills its own cell). Every gap is 2 wide and every step up
;; at most 2 tiles from where the hero can stand, except the tall post (3 above the fore deck,
;; 2 above the blaster post next to it) and the 3-tall blaster post at 44 (3 above the main
;; deck); tests/sim/airship-deck.test.ts runs every hero across.
